{"parentUuid":"b9067a23-b69a-418e-a2cb-03799a0e9186","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"c2b51eb0-d0e9-43cf-b431-42c05d49450b","version":"2.1.12","gitBranch":"alex/ent-53-improve-explain","slug":"wise-yawning-wand","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_018C4XyEj4sMYoKFtBDV5E5x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a really important architectural question. The user is pointing out that the relationships between sessions, checkpoints, and commits are complex and not 1:1:\n\n1. **Multiple sessions → one checkpoint**: Different chat sessions could work on the same uncommitted code, leading to a single checkpoint\n2. **One session → multiple commits**: A long session might result in several commits\n3. **Bundled changes**: If you don't commit often, a checkpoint might bundle many changes from different points in time\n4. **One session → multiple checkpoints**: A session's transcript gets split across checkpoints, so only part of the log is relevant to each\n\nThis means the current assumption of \"explain a session\" or \"explain a checkpoint\" as equivalent units is flawed.\n\nLet me think about the entities:\n\n- **Session**: A single Claude Code chat session (has a start time, transcript, prompts)\n- **Checkpoint**: A snapshot of code state + metadata (may span sessions, or be a slice of a session)\n- **Commit**: A git commit (may contain one or more checkpoints worth of work)\n\nFor review purposes (the use cases we're designing for), what do users actually want to understand?\n\nFor **self-review before commit**: \"What have I changed since my last commit?\" - this is about uncommitted work, which might span multiple sessions or be part of one session\n\nFor **team review**: \"What does this commit/PR represent?\" - this is about a commit, which might have been built up over multiple sessions\n\nThe question is: what's the right \"unit\" to explain?\n\nOptions:\n1. **Session-centric**: Explain what happened in a session (current approach, but transcript may not map cleanly to checkpoints)\n2. **Checkpoint-centric**: Explain what's in a specific checkpoint (code state + relevant portions of transcript)\n3. **Commit-centric**: Explain a commit (ties to `entire explain --commit`)\n4. **Work-unit-centric**: A new abstraction that tracks intent → outcome regardless of session/checkpoint boundaries\n\n\n5. **Diff-centric**: Focus on the actual code changes between two points, then pull relevant context from available transcripts\n\nI need to clarify with the user which mental model makes sense for their workflow and what they're actually trying to explain in practice.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57746,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":57746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXGCKShmqnFJPnhVZEzHQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"79c4ccb8-5be8-4159-996f-695b14425d98","timestamp":"2026-01-19T05:37:19.868Z"}
{"parentUuid":"79c4ccb8-5be8-4159-996f-695b14425d98","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"c2b51eb0-d0e9-43cf-b431-42c05d49450b","version":"2.1.12","gitBranch":"alex/ent-53-improve-explain","slug":"wise-yawning-wand","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_018C4XyEj4sMYoKFtBDV5E5x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is an important architectural question. Let me make sure I understand the current reality:\n\n| Relationship | Reality |\n|--------------|---------|\n| Session → Checkpoint | One session can span multiple checkpoints (transcript gets sliced) |\n| Checkpoint → Session | One checkpoint can have contributions from multiple sessions |\n| Session → Commit | One session can produce multiple commits |\n| Commit → Checkpoint | One commit bundles one or more checkpoints |\n\nSo there's no clean 1:1 mapping between these entities.\n\n**For the review use cases, what's the natural \"unit\" a user wants explained?**\n\n1. **Commit-centric** - \"What does this commit represent?\" (maps to team review/PR review)\n2. **Checkpoint-centric** - \"What's in this checkpoint?\" (maps to rewind points)\n3. **Session-centric** - \"What happened in this chat?\" (maps to self-review of a single interaction)\n4. **Work-in-progress** - \"What have I changed since last commit?\" (uncommitted work, potentially multi-session)\n\nOr maybe `explain` needs to support multiple of these with different entry points?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57746,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":57746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXGCKShmqnFJPnhVZEzHQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"664822da-01b9-43b0-b9bf-4bae94c1a927","timestamp":"2026-01-19T05:37:22.510Z"}
