{"parentUuid":"4f614057-9dcd-4b7c-8c21-1e45b88cfd42","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"c2b51eb0-d0e9-43cf-b431-42c05d49450b","version":"2.1.12","gitBranch":"alex/ent-53-improve-explain","slug":"wise-yawning-wand","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_015MHef1uprSLa7VTs3UVg4k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NNDDHnpKEsXm8hrp7ZnrdJ","name":"mcp__linear-server__create_comment","input":{"issueId":"ENT-53","body":"# Design: Clean Up Explain Output\n\n## Problem\n\n`entire explain` currently outputs all captured information, which is overwhelming. Users need a cleaner way to understand what happened during agent-driven development for self-review and team review.\n\n## Key Insight\n\nThe value of `explain` isn't duplicating commit messages - it's capturing what commits *can't*:\n- **The conversation** - the journey, alternatives considered, dead ends\n- **Discovered knowledge** - things learned during the session\n- **Friction points** - where the agent struggled, retries needed\n- **Cost** - token usage, time spent\n\nThis makes `explain` a **development journal/retrospective**, not a commit summary.\n\n## Design\n\n### Unit of Organization\n\n- **Branch** is the unit of review (matches PR paradigm)\n- **Checkpoints** are the logical units within a branch (checkpoint ≈ commit + metadata)\n- **Sessions** are de-emphasized (available for debugging/tracing)\n\n### Output Tiers\n\n**Default** (no flags):\n```\n$ entire explain\nBranch: alex/ent-53-clean-up-explain-output\nCheckpoints: 4 | Sessions: 3 | Total: 120k tokens (~$0.35)\n\nIntent: Improve `entire explain` output for human and AI readability\nOutcome: Implemented tiered output with AI-generated summaries, learnings, and friction tracking\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[abc123] 2026-01-19 10:30\n  Intent: Clean up explain output\n  Outcome: Added tiered output with --verbose/--full flags\n  Learnings: Pager already supported; go-git tree diffing slow on large repos\n  Friction: Streaming approach incompatible with pager\n  Cost: 45k tokens | 12 min\n\n[def456] 2026-01-19 14:15\n  Intent: Add AI-generated summaries\n  Outcome: Summaries stored with checkpoint metadata\n  Learnings: Small model sufficient for summarization\n  Friction: None\n  Cost: 30k tokens | 8 min\n```\n\n**Verbose** (`--verbose` / `-v`): Adds session IDs, original prompts, files changed, key decisions\n\n**Full** (`--full`): Adds complete transcript\n\n### Flags\n\n| Flag | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `--verbose` / `-v` | Add session IDs, original prompts, files, key decisions |\n| `--full` | Add complete transcript |\n| `--generate` | Generate/regenerate AI summaries (can run in background) |\n| `--checkpoint <id>` | Single checkpoint view |\n| `--session <id>` | Single session view (for debugging) |\n\n### AI-Generated Content\n\nFor each checkpoint, AI extracts from transcript:\n- **Intent** - distilled goal from original prompt(s)\n- **Outcome** - what was actually accomplished  \n- **Learnings** - discovered knowledge during the conversation\n- **Friction** - struggles, retries, dead ends\n\nFor the branch:\n- **Intent** - overarching goal across all checkpoints\n- **Outcome** - overall result\n\n### Summary Generation & Storage\n\n- **On-demand**: Use `--generate` flag to create summaries\n- **Lazy caching**: Once generated, stored with checkpoint metadata\n- **Background option**: Generation can run in separate process\n- **Future (ENT-96)**: Generate summaries automatically at checkpoint time\n\n### Fallback Behavior\n\nFor sessions/checkpoints without generated summaries:\n- Show raw prompt as \"Intent\" fallback\n- Show \"(run with --generate to create summary)\" for missing fields\n\n## Relationship to ENT-96\n\nThis design is compatible with [ENT-96](/issue/ENT-96) which proposes generating summaries at checkpoint time. The `--generate` flag provides the on-demand path for existing sessions, while ENT-96 will provide the proactive path for new sessions.\n\n## Open Questions / Future Work\n\n1. **Auto-commit strategy**: May need different handling due to more granular checkpoints\n2. **Batch generation**: `entire summarize --all` to generate for all sessions\n3. **Summary refresh**: When/how to regenerate if transcript changes"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":204,"cache_read_input_tokens":65000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":204,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXGHSbdL4mVHrpkr1ZfNV","type":"assistant","uuid":"a681b033-83f0-4259-896f-d94fb73eef21","timestamp":"2026-01-19T06:44:36.108Z"}
